{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And why is HaShem bringing us.</b> What have we sinned against Him that He exerted Himself through you to bring us to this? For they thought that all this was a deception on His part, born of His hatred toward them on account of their idols in Egypt or for some other cause, as He testified when He said: וַתֵּאָמְרוּ בְּשִׂנְאַת ה׳ אוֹתָנוּ הוֹצִיאָנוּ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם לָתֵת אוֹתָנוּ בְּיַד הָאֱמֹרִי לְהַשְׁמִידֵנוּ (Deuteronomy 1:27)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Rendered הִשְׁתַּדֵּל as 'exerted Himself'; the Hitpa'el of ש-ד-ל here connotes deliberate effort or striving to accomplish something."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:43.855795012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}